# Root README sync

When you change any README, also open and update the playground root `README.md`.

Check and update:

- Top bar: LinkedIn / X / Instagram on the **left**. Coverage only on **app** READMEs (top **right**). Not on the playground root or `app_starters/` index.
- Project cards in the root and `app_starters/`: heading left, that app's coverage badge on the **same line, far right**
- One-line summary under each card
- Card and header links (`README »`, folder `»`, coverage → `#test-coverage`)
- Header logo and tech-stack badges live once in playground `assets/` (`logo.png`, `badges/`). App READMEs point there with a relative path. Put the target URL on the badge line; do not add a `[flutter-url]:` footer.
- Tech-stack badges are **left**-aligned (`<div align="left">`) so wrapped rows start on the left. Do not center that row.
- Coverage images stay per app in `assets/coverage/`
- The **Coverage pipeline** section lives only in the playground root README. App READMEs point there. They must not say that `flutter test --coverage` updates the badge SVGs; that command is Gutters/`lcov.info` only. SVGs refresh on playground **commit** (hooks). On **push**, GitHub Actions regenerates every app in `playground_apps` and **commits + pushes** if the images or percent still differ.
- The **Packages** table if a `pubspec.yaml` added, removed, or replaced a package
- Architecture notes only if the folder approach actually changed

Do not copy the **Coverage pipeline** or **Badges** sections into app READMEs. Point to the root sections.

```
# ❌ BAD — leave the root card stale after renaming a starter
### Old Name »

# ✅ GOOD — same change in the app README and the root card
<h3>
  <a href="app_starters/new_name/">New Name »</a>
  <a href="app_starters/new_name/README.md#test-coverage"><img align="right" src="app_starters/new_name/assets/coverage/badge.svg" alt="Coverage"></a>
</h3>
```
